### Relay API examples — VS Code REST Client format
### Start the server first: npm run server
### Replace the token if you set RELAY_API_KEY to something else.

@base = http://localhost:4000
@token = rly_live_demo
@key = demo-request-001

### Public health check
GET {{base}}/v1/health

### OpenAPI contract
GET {{base}}/v1/openapi.json

### Dashboard aggregate consumed by Atlas Analytics
GET {{base}}/v1/analytics/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List events (first page)
GET {{base}}/v1/events?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an event
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{
  "type": "event.created",
  "data": { "source": "rest-client", "order": 1042 }
}

### Repeat the POST above with the same Idempotency-Key:
### the original event is replayed instead of duplicated.

### Retrieve one event (copy an id from a list response)
GET {{base}}/v1/events/evt_seed01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete an event
DELETE {{base}}/v1/events/evt_seed01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid request — demonstrates the error envelope
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": {} }

### Unauthorized request — demonstrates 401 shape
GET {{base}}/v1/events
